import static diagnosticTables.*;

/**
 * Carbon transport model (XL port of the L+C coupled phloem/xylem framework).
 *
 * <p><b>Scope</b> — Implements the Seleznyova & Hanan (2018) analytical + computational
 * approach for mass transport through the phloem, coupled to xylem hydraulics, on top of
 * a GroIMP/XL plant graph. The solver operates in the carbon-potential domain
 * Φ (denoted {@code cp}) with {@code cp = 0.5 * c^2}, where {@code c} is phloem carbon
 * concentration (g C cm⁻³). Nonlinear organ loading/unloading is linearised per Newton step as
 * {@code j(Φ) ≈ a + b · Φ}, with {@code a,b} assembled into per-node branch terms.</p>
 *
 * <p><b>Key conventions</b>
 * <ul>
 *   <li><b>Potential:</b> {@code cp} is carbon potential Φ; {@code cpt}/{@code cpb} are top/bottom
 *       potentials of a transport element.</li>
 *   <li><b>Flux sign:</b> {@code j} is net mass carbon flux (gC·h⁻¹). Positive {@code j} = unloading
 *       from phloem to the organ (sink). Negative {@code j} = loading from organ to phloem (source).</li>
 *   <li><b>Linearisation:</b> Each organ computes {@code sink_source_a} and {@code sink_source_b},
 *       then branch-level accumulators {@code branch_flux_a}, {@code branch_flux_b} are folded
 *       upstream per axis.</li>
 *   <li><b>Resistance/xylem coupling:</b> Transport update uses local phloem resistance {@code r}
 *       and xylem pull term {@code xp}; Munch counter flow is updated from branch flux.</li>
 * </ul></p>
 *
 * <p><b>Solver loop</b> (one time step)
 * <ol>
 *   <li>{@code linearise(pb, context)} — compute per-organ (a,b).</li>
 *   <li>{@code updateBranchFlux(pb, context)} — fold (a,b) upstream by axis/root to the PlantBase.</li>
 *   <li>{@code updateCarbonPotential(pb, context)} — UNFOLD potentials from PlantBase to its children.</li>
 *   <li>{@code updateFlow(pb, context)} — update organ fluxes j = a + b·cpt and the solve residual.</li>
 *   <li>{@code updateResistence(pb)} — refresh phloem resistance and related transport params.</li>
 *   <li>Repeat 1–5 until the residual is at most {@code MAXERROR} or the iteration limit is exceeded.</li>
 *   <li>{@code updateCarbonStatus(pb)} — compute per-organ sugar, loading/leakage/unloading and Mcf.</li>
 * </ol></p>
 *
 * <p><b>Debugging</b> — Verbose printing is guarded by the global {@code debug_CT} flag; some summaries
 * print unconditionally where noted. The fold/unfold passes use step ticks to warn on double writes.</p>
 *
 * <p><b>Units</b> — Fluxes are g C h⁻¹ unless stated. {@code cp} in g² C cm⁻⁶, concentrations in g C cm⁻³
 * (or converted sugar units where noted). Constants are documented inline.</p>
 *
 *******************************************************************************************
 * Revised carbon transport linearisation using sugar-domain source/sink responses.
 *
 * <p><b>Purpose.</b>
 * The carbon transport (CT) solver still operates in the carbon-potential domain,
 * where:
 * <pre>
 *     Phi = cp = 0.5 * c^2
 * </pre>
 *
 * with {@code c} being phloem carbon concentration. The solver requires each
 * organ exchange flux to be locally linearised as:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     j(Phi) ~= a + b * Phi
 * </pre>
 *
 * where {@code j} is the net carbon exchange flux between the organ and the
 * phloem. Positive {@code j} represents unloading from phloem to organ
 * (sink behaviour), while negative {@code j} represents loading from organ
 * to phloem (source behaviour).
 *
 * <p>The revised implementation changes the biological response domain of
 * source loading and sink unloading. Instead of evaluating the loading and
 * unloading response functions directly in {@code Phi}-space, the model now:
 *
 * <ol>
 *   <li>converts local carbon potential {@code Phi} to phloem carbon concentration,</li>
 *   <li>converts phloem carbon concentration to phloem sugar concentration,</li>
 *   <li>evaluates source/sink response functions in sugar concentration space,</li>
 *   <li>uses the chain rule to obtain derivatives with respect to {@code Phi},</li>
 *   <li>builds the standard CT linear coefficients {@code a} and {@code b}.</li>
 * </ol>
 *
 * <p>This preserves the analytical/iterative CT solver structure while making
 * organ-level source and sink responses more consistent with the CP/common-pool
 * carbon allocation formulation, where limitation functions are naturally
 * parameterised in sugar or concentration space.
 *
 * <h3>Conversion from carbon potential to sugar concentration</h3>
 *
 * <p>The local carbon potential is first converted to carbon concentration:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     c = sqrt(2 * Phi)
 * </pre>
 *
 * and then converted to phloem sugar concentration through:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     sugar = convertPhloemCtoSugar(c)
 * </pre>
 *
 * This conversion is wrapped by {@code sugarFromCp(cp)}. The derivative used
 * for the chain rule assumes that sugar concentration is proportional to carbon
 * concentration:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     dSugar/dPhi = sugar / (2 * Phi)
 * </pre>
 *
 * Because this derivative becomes numerically sensitive near {@code Phi = 0},
 * the implementation applies lower bounds to {@code cp} and sugar concentration
 * using {@code CT_CP_MIN} and {@code CT_SUGAR_MIN}.
 *
 * <h3>Sink unloading response in sugar space</h3>
 *
 * <p>Sink unloading is evaluated using a Michaelis-Menten-like response:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     f(sugar; Km) = sugar / (Km + sugar) + epsilon
 * </pre>
 *
 * where {@code Km} is the sugar-domain half-saturation parameter for the
 * corresponding sink component. Different sink components can use different
 * {@code Km} values, for example:
 *
 * <ul>
 *   <li>{@code km_pri} for primary structural growth demand,</li>
 *   <li>{@code km_sec} for secondary structural growth demand,</li>
 *   <li>{@code km_res} for reserve storage demand,</li>
 *   <li>{@code KM_MTNCE} for maintenance demand,</li>
 *   <li>{@code km_res} for fine-root exudation in the current implementation.</li>
 * </ul>
 *
 * <p>The derivative in sugar space is:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     df/dSugar = Km / (Km + sugar)^2
 * </pre>
 *
 * The CT solver needs the derivative with respect to {@code Phi}, therefore:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     df/dPhi = df/dSugar * dSugar/dPhi
 *             = Km / (Km + sugar)^2 * sugar / (2 * Phi)
 * </pre>
 *
 * This is implemented by {@code dSinkUnloading_fromSugar_dcp(cp, kmSugar)}.
 *
 * <h3>Source loading response in sugar space</h3>
 *
 * <p>Source loading is evaluated using a logistic response in sugar space:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     g(sugar) = -1 / (1 + exp(b * (sugar - sugar0)))
 * </pre>
 *
 * where {@code b} is the logistic slope and {@code sugar0} is the sugar-domain
 * inflection point. The negative sign preserves the existing CT convention that
 * source loading into the phloem is a negative exchange flux.
 *
 * <p>The derivative in sugar space is:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     dg/dSugar = b * exp(b * (sugar - sugar0))
 *                 / (1 + exp(b * (sugar - sugar0)))^2
 * </pre>
 *
 * and the derivative required by the CT solver is:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     dg/dPhi = dg/dSugar * dSugar/dPhi
 *             = dg/dSugar * sugar / (2 * Phi)
 * </pre>
 *
 * This is implemented by {@code dSourceLoading_fromSugar_dcp(cp, bSugar, c0Sugar)}.
 * The exponential argument is clamped to avoid overflow.
 *
 * <h3>Organ-level Taylor linearisation</h3>
 *
 * <p>For each organ and each Newton iteration, the current potential
 * {@code Phi0 = o.cpt} is used as the expansion point. For a generic response
 * function {@code h(Phi)}, the first-order Taylor expansion is:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     h(Phi) ~= h(Phi0) + h'(Phi0) * (Phi - Phi0)
 * </pre>
 *
 * Multiplying by the corresponding potential flux/demand term {@code PT} gives:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     j(Phi) ~= PT * (h0 - Phi0 * hPrime) + PT * hPrime * Phi
 * </pre>
 *
 * Therefore:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     a = PT * (h0 - Phi0 * hPrime)
 *     b = PT * hPrime
 * </pre>
 *
 * <p>For sink components, {@code h} is the sugar-domain unloading response
 * converted back to {@code d/dPhi}. For source loading, {@code h} is the
 * sugar-domain logistic loading response converted back to {@code d/dPhi}.
 *
 * <p>The final organ coefficients are:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     sink_source_a = mgTogram * (sum(sinkA) + loadA)
 *     sink_source_b = mgTogram * (sum(sinkB) + loadB)
 * </pre>
 *
 * and the organ exchange flux used by the CT solver is:
 *
 * <pre>
 *     j = sink_source_a + sink_source_b * cpt
 * </pre>
 *
 * <h3>Whole-plant CT calculation flow</h3>
 *
 * <p>The revised sugar-domain response functions are used inside the existing
 * CT solve sequence:
 *
 * <ol>
 *   <li>{@code linearise(pb, context)} computes local {@code sink_source_a} and
 *       {@code sink_source_b} for each organ.</li>
 *   <li>{@code updateBranchFlux(pb, context)} folds local coefficients upstream through
 *       the plant graph to obtain branch-level {@code branch_flux_a} and
 *       {@code branch_flux_b}.</li>
 *   <li>{@code updateCarbonPotential(pb, context)} solves/unfolds carbon potential from
 *       {@code PlantBase} to downstream transport elements using branch
 *       coefficients, phloem resistance, and xylem-pull terms.</li>
 *   <li>{@code updateFlow(pb, context)} recomputes local fluxes as
 *       {@code j = a + b * cpt} and accumulates the convergence residual.</li>
 *   <li>{@code updateResistence(pb)} updates concentration-dependent resistance
 *       and transport parameters from the latest local carbon concentration.</li>
 *   <li>The loop repeats until the convergence residual is at most {@code MAXERROR} or the iteration
 *       guard is reached.</li>
 *   <li>{@code updateCarbonStatus(pb)} updates final organ sugar concentration,
 *       carbon allocation state, carbon flux, and Munch counter-flow terms.</li>
 * </ol>
 *
 * <h3>Parameter interpretation</h3>
 *
 * <p>After this revision, parameters passed to {@code SinkUnloading_fromSugar}
 * and {@code SourceLoading_fromSugar} are interpreted in sugar concentration
 * space, not carbon-potential space. In particular, the legacy parameter name
 * {@code sourceLoading_cp} may be misleading when used as the logistic
 * inflection argument in {@code SourceLoading_fromSugar}; biologically and
 * numerically it should now be interpreted as a sugar-domain threshold.
 *
 * <p>Recommended future cleanup: rename {@code sourceLoading_cp} to a clearer
 * name such as {@code sourceLoadingSugarThreshold} or
 * {@code sourceLoading_sugar_c0}, while preserving backward compatibility in
 * the JSON/config loader if required.
 *
 * <h3>Numerical guards</h3>
 *
 * <p>The revision relies on the following guards:
 *
 * <ul>
 *   <li>{@code CT_CP_MIN}: lower bound for carbon potential before conversion,</li>
 *   <li>{@code CT_SUGAR_MIN}: lower bound for sugar concentration in derivative calculations,</li>
 *   <li>{@code CT_DERIV_MAX}: upper bound for source/sink derivatives with respect to {@code Phi}.</li>
 * </ul>
 *
 * <p>These guards are required because {@code dSugar/dPhi = sugar / (2 * Phi)}
 * is sensitive near zero carbon potential and can otherwise produce unstable
 * Newton coefficients.
 *
 * @see #SinkUnloading_fromSugar(double, double)
 * @see #dSinkUnloading_fromSugar_dcp(double, double)
 * @see #SourceLoading_fromSugar(double, double, double)
 * @see #dSourceLoading_fromSugar_dcp(double, double, double)
 * @see #lineariseOrgan(GrowingOrgan)
 * @see #linearise(PlantBase, CarbonTransportSolveContext)
 * @see #updateBranchFlux(PlantBase, CarbonTransportSolveContext)
 * @see #updateCarbonPotential(PlantBase, CarbonTransportSolveContext)
 * @see #updateFlow(PlantBase, CarbonTransportSolveContext)
 * @see #updateResistence(PlantBase)
 * @see #updateCarbonStatus(PlantBase)
 * @author  Port: Junqi Zhu {@code <junqi.zhu@plantandfood.co.nz>}
 * @since   2021 updated on 2025-08
 */


/* #### defines pertinents for the carbon transport model ##################*/
global double INFTY     = 1e10;      // very large number
global double EPSILON   = 1.0/INFTY; // very small number different from zero
global double MAXERROR  = 1e-5;      // error threshold for evaluating carbon flow

global boolean debug_CT = false;

// Retained only so saved GroIMP projects containing the former globals load cleanly.
// Active solves use CarbonTransportSolveContext and never read or write these fields.
global double Serror = 0.0;
global int error_count = 0;

/** Per-call mutable state for one plant's carbon-transport solve. */
private class CarbonTransportSolveContext {
  double convergenceError = 0.0;
  int iterationCount = 0;
  int foldStep = 0;
  int unfoldStep = 0;

  double leafA = 0.0, leafB = 0.0, leafJ = 0.0;
  double petioleA = 0.0, petioleB = 0.0, petioleJ = 0.0;
  double shootA = 0.0, shootB = 0.0, shootJ = 0.0;
  double fineRootA = 0.0, fineRootB = 0.0, fineRootJ = 0.0;
  double structuralRootA = 0.0, structuralRootB = 0.0, structuralRootJ = 0.0;
  double fruitA = 0.0, fruitB = 0.0, fruitJ = 0.0;
}

// CT response is evaluated in sugar concentration domain and linearised d/dPhi.
static final double CT_CP_MIN = 1e-10;
static final double CT_SUGAR_MIN = 1e-9;
static final double CT_DERIV_MAX = 1e9;
static final double CT_PHI_FLOOR = 1e-8;
// g C h-1 per unit Phi; guards only numerically degenerate folded boundaries.
static final double CT_PB_B_ABS_MIN = 1e-12;

// defines pertinent to test case 
// constant source and sink
global double SOURCEj = 0; //-0.4;  	    // [g h-1] maximum initial influx from the source (for initialization of the system)  
//global double SINKj = 0.5;            // [g h-1] maximun possible influx into the terminal sink
 
global double SOURCEcp = 0.0002;   //calculate carbon potential for sourceLoading_cp; initial value is important; far from the answer can cause nan value
global double initial_c0 = Math.sqrt(2*SOURCEcp);
// defines pertinent to phloem resistance
global double R0 = 0.847E-3;	  // [MPa cm-4 h] //resistance at zero phloem sugar concentration
global double R_ct = 0.024298245614035;  // [MPa cm3 g-1 K-1] //universal gas constant
//global double Tk = 293.15;             // [K]

// defines pertinent to water potential
//global double Rx = 1.0063894024855E-6;          // [cm-4 h] resistance per unit length of xylem
global double MolalVolumeSucrose = 0.6301;      // [g-1 cm3]  



/* #### defines the functions for the carbon transport model ##################*/

/**
 * CP-style unloading response evaluated in sugar concentration space, then used by
 * the CT Phi-domain solver through Taylor linearisation in {@link #lineariseOrgan}.
 *
 * @param cp carbon potential Phi (not common-pool concentration)
 * @param kmSugar half-saturation sugar concentration (g sugar cm^-3)
 * @return unloading activity in sugar domain (unitless multiplier before PT scaling)
 */
static double SinkUnloading_fromSugar(double cp, double kmSugar) {
    double cpEff = Math.max(CT_CP_MIN, cp);
    double sugar = sugarFromCp(cpEff);
    if (Double.isNaN(sugar) || sugar < 0.0) {
        sugar = 0.0;
    }
    double km = kmSugar;
    if (Double.isNaN(km) || km <= 0.0) {
        km = CT_SUGAR_MIN;
    }
    return sugar / (km + sugar) + 1e-6;
}

/**
 * Chain-rule derivative dS/dPhi for {@link #SinkUnloading_fromSugar}.
 *
 * @param cp carbon potential Phi (not common-pool concentration)
 * @param kmSugar half-saturation sugar concentration (g sugar cm^-3)
 * @return dS/dPhi with numerical guards near Phi=0
 */
static double dSinkUnloading_fromSugar_dcp(double cp, double kmSugar) {
    double cpEff = Math.max(CT_CP_MIN, cp);
    double sugar = sugarFromCp(cpEff);
    if (Double.isNaN(sugar) || sugar < CT_SUGAR_MIN) {
        sugar = CT_SUGAR_MIN;
    }
    double km = kmSugar;
    if (Double.isNaN(km) || km <= 0.0) {
        km = CT_SUGAR_MIN;
    }
    double dS_dSugar = km / ((km + sugar) * (km + sugar));
    double dSugar_dCp = sugar / (2.0 * cpEff);
    double out = dS_dSugar * dSugar_dCp;
    if (Double.isNaN(out) || out < 0.0) {
        out = 0.0;
    }
    if (out > CT_DERIV_MAX) {
        out = CT_DERIV_MAX;
    }
    return out + 1e-20;
}


/**
 * CP-style source loading response evaluated in the sugar concentration domain.
 * Negative return value preserves the existing source-loading sign convention.
 *
 * @param cp carbon potential Phi (not common-pool concentration)
 * @param bSugar logistic slope in sugar concentration space
 * @param c0Sugar logistic inflection sugar concentration (g sugar cm^-3)
 * @return loading activity (negative, before PT scaling)
 */
static double SourceLoading_fromSugar(double cp, double bSugar, double c0Sugar) {
    double cpEff = Math.max(CT_CP_MIN, cp);
    double sugar = sugarFromCp(cpEff);
    if (Double.isNaN(sugar) || sugar < 0.0) {
        sugar = 0.0;
    }
    double expArg = bSugar * (sugar - c0Sugar);
    if (expArg > 100.0) expArg = 100.0;
    if (expArg < -100.0) expArg = -100.0;
    double e = Math.exp(expArg);
    return -1.0 / (1.0 + e);
}

/**
 * Chain-rule derivative dLoading/dPhi for {@link #SourceLoading_fromSugar}.
 *
 * @param cp carbon potential Phi (not common-pool concentration)
 * @param bSugar logistic slope in sugar concentration space
 * @param c0Sugar logistic inflection sugar concentration (g sugar cm^-3)
 * @return dLoading/dPhi, clamped for numerical stability
 */
static double dSourceLoading_fromSugar_dcp(double cp, double bSugar, double c0Sugar) {
    double cpEff = Math.max(CT_CP_MIN, cp);
    double sugar = sugarFromCp(cpEff);
    if (Double.isNaN(sugar) || sugar < CT_SUGAR_MIN) {
        sugar = CT_SUGAR_MIN;
    }
    double expArg = bSugar * (sugar - c0Sugar);
    if (expArg > 700.0) expArg = 700.0;
    if (expArg < -700.0) expArg = -700.0;
    double e = Math.exp(expArg);
    double dg_dSugar = bSugar * e / ((1.0 + e) * (1.0 + e));
    double dSugar_dCp = sugar / (2.0 * cpEff);
    double out = dg_dSugar * dSugar_dCp;
    if (Double.isNaN(out)) {
        out = 0.0;
    }
    if (Math.abs(out) > CT_DERIV_MAX) {
        out = Math.signum(out) * CT_DERIV_MAX;
    }
    return out;
}

/////////ALTERNATIVE FUNCTION IF YOU WANT TO DO DERIVATIVE REGARDING TO C//////////

// phloem resistance ratio R_ct/R0
/**
 * Empirical phloem resistance ratio as a function of phloem carbon concentration.
 *
 * @param cab phloem carbon concentration (g C cm⁻³)
 * @return R_ct/R0 ratio (dimensionless)
 */
static double PhloemResistanceRatio_sucrose (double cab) 
{
  double  k1 = 0.19961;
  double  k2 = 1.00954;
  double  k3 = -2.2249;
  double  k4 = 1.2776; 
  return (1.0+k1*cab+k2*cab*cab)/(1.0+k3*cab+k4*cab*cab);			 
} 

//Osmotic pressure ratio P/RT
/**
 * Osmotic pressure ratio P/(R·T) as a function of phloem carbon concentration.
 *
 * @param cab phloem carbon concentration (g C cm⁻³)
 * @return P/(R·T) (dimensionless)
 @FIXME fix the effects of sorbital form on pressure ratio. 
 * double cabEq = cabTotal_gC_cm3 * ((1.0 - fSor)*1.0 + fSor*MOL_EQ_FACTOR);
 * double P_over_RT = PressureRatio(cabEq);

 */
static double PressureRatio (double cab) 
{
  double  a = 1.03913;
  double  b = 0.86536;
  double  c = 5.2465;
  //quick scalling for the osmotic potential ratio to RT
  double cabEq = cab * ((1.0 - FRACTION_SORBITOL)*1.0 + FRACTION_SORBITOL* (MOL_SURCROSE/MOL_SORBITOL));
  return (a + b*cabEq + c*cabEq*cabEq);			 
}
// ---- constants you already have (names are examples) ----
static final double CF_SUC = CARBON_FRACTION_SUCROSE;   // ~0.42 gC/g sucrose
static final double CF_SOR = CARBON_FRACTION_SORBITOL;  // ~0.40 gC/g sorbitol
static final double RHO_WATER_25C = 1.0;               // g/cm3, good 5–25% w/w


// Minimal η/ηwater fits at 25 °C vs weight fraction w (0–0.3). Replace when you fit CRC points.
static double etaRelSucrose(double w){ return 1.0 + 2.4*w + 12.0*w*w; }
static double etaRelSorbitol(double w){ return 1.0 + 1.6*w + 6.5*w*w; }

// helpers
static double soluteMassPerCm3(double cab, double carbonFrac){ return cab / Math.max(1e-12, carbonFrac); }
static double weightFraction(double gs){ return gs / (gs + RHO_WATER_25C); } // gs = g solute per cm3

// FRACTION_SORBITOL in [0,1]
static double PhloemResistanceRatio_mixture(double cab, double FRACTION_SORBITOL){
    // split carbon between species
    double cabSor = cab * FRACTION_SORBITOL;
    double cabSuc = cab * (1.0 - FRACTION_SORBITOL);

    // convert to g solute / cm3 (approx density)
    double gsSor = soluteMassPerCm3(cabSor, CF_SOR);
    double gsSuc = soluteMassPerCm3(cabSuc, CF_SUC);
    double gsTot = gsSor + gsSuc;
    double wTot  = weightFraction(gsTot);     // overall wt% as fraction 0–1

    // log-additivity for viscosity of two non-electrolytes (Grunberg–Nissan with G12≈0)
    double xSuc = (gsTot > 0) ? gsSuc / gsTot : 0.0;
    double xSor = 1.0 - xSuc;
    double etaRelMix = Math.exp(xSuc*Math.log(etaRelSucrose(wTot)) + xSor*Math.log(etaRelSorbitol(wTot)));

    // reference (what your k1..k4 implicitly used)
    double etaRelRef = etaRelSucrose(wTot);

    // scale sucrose baseline by viscosity ratio
    return PhloemResistanceRatio_sucrose(cab) * (etaRelMix / Math.max(1e-12, etaRelRef));
}

/** cp → phloem sugar concentration (g sugar cm⁻³). 
 * Convert carbon potential to sugar concentration (model’s sugar unit).
 *
 * @param cp carbon potential Φ (≥0)
 * @return sugar concentration (g sugar cm⁻³)
 */
static double sugarFromCp(double cp) {
  double c = Math.sqrt(Math.max(0.0, 2.0 * cp));     // c = √(2cp), guard cp≥0
  return convertPhloemCtoSugar((double) c);
}
/** KM in sugar domain → KM in cp domain: cp = 0.5 * c² (with c in gC cm⁻³). 
 * Convert Michaelis constant from sugar-concentration space to potential space.
 *
 * @param km_sugar KM in sugar domain (g sugar cm⁻³)
 * @return KM in cp domain (g² C cm⁻⁶)
 */
static double kmSugarToCp(double km_sugar) {
  double c = convertSugarToPhloemC((double) km_sugar); // sugar → phloem C
  return 0.5 * c * c;
}



/**
 * Linearise sinks and sources for a single organ (fills sink_source_a/b).
 *
 * <p><b>Purpose</b> — Compute the first-order (Taylor) linearisation of the organ’s
 * net phloem exchange <code>j(Φ)</code> around the current carbon potential
 * <code>Φ = cp = o.cpt</code>, so the solver can use
 * <code>j ≈ a + b · Φ</code> within a Newton step.</p>
 *
 * <p><b>Inputs used</b>
 * <ul>
 *   <li><code>o.cpt</code> (top-side carbon potential Φ) and <code>o.cpb</code> (bottom-side guard).</li>
 *   <li>Organ PT multipliers: <code>o.loading_PT</code>, <code>o.structureDM_PRI_PT</code>,
 *       <code>o.structureDM_SEC_PT</code>, <code>o.reserveDM_PT</code>, <code>o.maintenanceDM_PT</code>.</li>
 *   <li>Km-like parameters (in sugar domain) converted to Φ-domain via
 *       <code>cp = 0.5 · c²</code>: <code>o.km_pri</code>, <code>o.km_sec</code>, <code>o.km_res</code>,
 *       and <code>KM_MTNCE</code>.</li>
 *   <li>Model kernels in Φ-domain: <code>SourceLoading(Φ,…)</code>,
 *       <code>dSourceLoading_dcp(Φ,…)</code>, <code>SinkUnloading(Φ,q)</code>,
 *       <code>dSinkUnloading_dcp(Φ,q)</code>.</li>
 * </ul></p>
 *
 * <p><b>Outputs / side effects</b>
 * <ul>
 *   <li>Sets <code>o.sink_source_a</code> and <code>o.sink_source_b</code> (same mass-flow units as <code>j</code>;
 *       <code>b</code> is “per-Φ” slope). Positive values contribute to unloading (sink), negative to loading (source).</li>
 *   <li>Clamps invalid potentials and applies small-Φ safeguards for derivative stability.</li>
 *   <li>Optionally prints a per-organ debug_CT line when <code>debug_CT</code> is true for selected organ classes.</li>
 * </ul></p>
 *
 * <p><b>Definition of the linear terms</b>
 * <ul>
 *   <li><b>a (intercept)</b>:
 *     <code>a = j(Φ₀) − Φ₀ · j′(Φ₀)</code>, evaluated at <code>Φ₀ = o.cpt</code>.
 *     In code this is the sum over unloading components
 *     <code>PT · (SinkUnloading(Φ₀,q) − Φ₀ · dSinkUnloading_dcp(Φ₀,q))</code>
 *     plus the analogous loading term
 *     <code>o.loading_PT · (SourceLoading(Φ₀,…) − Φ₀ · dSourceLoading_dcp(Φ₀,…))</code>.
 *   </li>
 *   <li><b>b (slope)</b>:
 *     <code>b = j′(Φ₀)</code>, the derivative w.r.t. Φ at <code>Φ₀</code>.
 *     In code this is the sum over unloading components
 *     <code>PT · dSinkUnloading_dcp(Φ₀,q)</code> plus the loading derivative
 *     <code>o.loading_PT · dSourceLoading_dcp(Φ₀,…)</code>.
 *   </li>
 * </ul>
 * This yields the local linear form <code>j(Φ) ≈ a + b · Φ</code> that the transport solver
 * uses to assemble branch fluxes and update potentials.</p>
 */
static void lineariseOrgan(GrowingOrgan o) {
  if (o == null) return;

  // Basic guards
  if (Double.isNaN(o.cpb) || o.cpb < 0.0) o.cpb = 1e-5;
  if (Double.isNaN(o.cpt) || o.cpt < 0.0) o.cpt = 1e-5;
  // Current state (Φ-domain uses cp = c^2/2)
  double cp = o.cpt;                           // carbon potential Φ at organ
  double sugar = sugarFromCp(cp);              // current sugar (used by organ to update PT)
  
  
  //o.calcPTCTRAM(sugar);                        // update organ-specific PT params from sugar
  o.updateCarbonAllocation(sugar);
  // --- Source (loading) linearisation: sugar-domain response, a + b * cp.
  double loadA = 0.0, loadB = 0.0;
  if (o.loading_PT > 0.0) {
    double cp_eff = (cp > CT_CP_MIN) ? cp : CT_CP_MIN;
    double g0 = SourceLoading_fromSugar(cp_eff, sourceLoading_b, sourceLoading_cp);
    double dg = dSourceLoading_fromSugar_dcp(cp_eff, sourceLoading_b, sourceLoading_cp);
    loadA = o.loading_PT * (g0 - cp_eff * dg);
    loadB = o.loading_PT * dg;
  }

  double kPRI = o.km_pri;
  double kSEC = o.km_sec;
  double kRES = o.km_res;
  double kMNT = KM_MTNCE;
  double fPRI = SinkUnloading_fromSugar(cp, kPRI);
  double fSEC = SinkUnloading_fromSugar(cp, kSEC);
  double fRES = SinkUnloading_fromSugar(cp, kRES);
  double fMNT = SinkUnloading_fromSugar(cp, kMNT);
  double dPRI = dSinkUnloading_fromSugar_dcp(cp, kPRI);
  double dSEC = dSinkUnloading_fromSugar_dcp(cp, kSEC);
  double dRES = dSinkUnloading_fromSugar_dcp(cp, kRES);
  double dMNT = dSinkUnloading_fromSugar_dcp(cp, kMNT);
  double sA_pri = o.structureDM_PRI_PT * (fPRI - cp * dPRI);
  double sA_sec = o.structureDM_SEC_PT * (fSEC - cp * dSEC);
  double sA_res = o.reserveDM_PT       * (fRES - cp * dRES);
  double sA_mnt = o.maintenanceDM_PT   * (fMNT - cp * dMNT);
  double sB_pri = o.structureDM_PRI_PT * dPRI;
  double sB_sec = o.structureDM_SEC_PT * dSEC;
  double sB_res = o.reserveDM_PT       * dRES;
  double sB_mnt = o.maintenanceDM_PT   * dMNT;

  // --- Exudation guarded via polymorphic getter (only FineRoot returns >0) ---
	double sA_exu = 0.0, sB_exu = 0.0;
	double exuPT  = o.getExudationPT();   // mg C per step; 0 for non-root organs
	if (exuPT > 0.0 && !Double.isNaN(exuPT)) {
    double fEXU = SinkUnloading_fromSugar(cp, o.km_res);
    double dEXU = dSinkUnloading_fromSugar_dcp(cp, o.km_res);
		sA_exu = exuPT * (fEXU - cp * dEXU);
		sB_exu = exuPT * dEXU;
	}

	// sums
	double sinkA = (sA_pri + sA_sec + sA_res + sA_mnt + sA_exu);
	double sinkB = (sB_pri + sB_sec + sB_res + sB_mnt + sB_exu);

  // Combine sources + sinks, convert units once here
  o.sink_source_a = mgTogram * (sinkA + loadA);
  o.sink_source_b = mgTogram * (sinkB + loadB);

  if (debug_CT && (o instanceof Trunk || o instanceof Cordon || o instanceof StructuralRoot || o instanceof FruitService)) {
    println(o.getClass().getSimpleName()
      + " loadPT=" + o.loading_PT
      + " priPT="  + o.structureDM_PRI_PT
      + " secPT="  + o.structureDM_SEC_PT
      + " resPT="  + o.reserveDM_PT
      + " mntPT="  + o.maintenanceDM_PT
      + " cp="     + cp
      + " | loadA=" + loadA + " loadB=" + loadB
      + " | priA="  + sA_pri + " priB=" + sB_pri
      + " | secA="  + sA_sec + " secB=" + sB_sec
      + " | resA="  + sA_res + " resB=" + sB_res
      + " | mntA="  + sA_mnt + " mntB=" + sB_mnt
      + " | A=" + (sinkA + loadA)
      + " | B=" + (sinkB + loadB));
  }
}


/* Carbon Dynamics Phases defined as groups --------------------------------- */

//group Linearise: // linearise equations for sinks/sources 
//left to right
/**
 * Linearises the sink/source relationships for all {@link GrowingOrgan} instances in the graph.
 * <p>
 * This method:
 * <ul>
 *   <li>Resets diagnostic accumulators for A/B coefficients and fluxes.</li>
 *   <li>Invokes {@link #lineariseOrgan(GrowingOrgan)} on each organ to compute per-organ
 *       linearised coefficients for sink and source terms.</li>
 *   <li>Accumulates totals per organ type for debugging and diagnostics.</li>
 *   <li>Optionally prints the per-class totals if {@code debug_CT} is enabled.</li>
 * </ul>
 * The linearisation results are stored in each organ's {@code sink_source_a} and {@code sink_source_b}
 * fields, and also copied to {@code branch_flux_a} and {@code branch_flux_b}.
 */
static void linearise(PlantBase pb, CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx) [
    {
        ctx.leafA = ctx.leafB = ctx.leafJ = 0.0;
        ctx.petioleA = ctx.petioleB = ctx.petioleJ = 0.0;
        ctx.shootA = ctx.shootB = ctx.shootJ = 0.0;
        ctx.fineRootA = ctx.fineRootB = ctx.fineRootJ = 0.0;
        ctx.structuralRootA = ctx.structuralRootB = ctx.structuralRootJ = 0.0;
        ctx.fruitA = ctx.fruitB = ctx.fruitJ = 0.0;
    }

    g:GrowingOrgan, (
        g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) ::> {
    	
        // Perform per-organ sink/source linearisation
        lineariseOrgan(g);

        // Store branch fluxes for later use
        g.branch_flux_a = g.sink_source_a;
        g.branch_flux_b = g.sink_source_b;

        // Accumulate diagnostics by organ type
        double jTerm = g.sink_source_a + g.sink_source_b * g.cpt;

        if (g instanceof Leaf) {
            ctx.leafA += g.sink_source_a; ctx.leafB += g.sink_source_b; ctx.leafJ += jTerm;
        } else if (g instanceof Petiole) {
            ctx.petioleA += g.sink_source_a; ctx.petioleB += g.sink_source_b; ctx.petioleJ += jTerm;
        } else if (g instanceof Internode || g instanceof Cordon || g instanceof Trunk) {
            ctx.shootA += g.sink_source_a; ctx.shootB += g.sink_source_b; ctx.shootJ += jTerm;
        } else if (g instanceof FineRoot) {
            ctx.fineRootA += g.sink_source_a; ctx.fineRootB += g.sink_source_b; ctx.fineRootJ += jTerm;
        } else if (g instanceof StructuralRoot) {
            ctx.structuralRootA += g.sink_source_a; ctx.structuralRootB += g.sink_source_b; ctx.structuralRootJ += jTerm;
        } else if (g instanceof FruitService) {
            ctx.fruitA += g.sink_source_a; ctx.fruitB += g.sink_source_b; ctx.fruitJ += jTerm;
        }
    }

    {
        if (debug_CT) {
            println(
                "DEBUG A/B by class   A            B            j\n" +
                "Leaf:        " + ctx.leafA + "  " + ctx.leafB + "  " + ctx.leafJ + "\n" +
                "Petiole:     " + ctx.petioleA + "  " + ctx.petioleB + "  " + ctx.petioleJ + "\n" +
                "Shoot(core): " + ctx.shootA + "  " + ctx.shootB + "  " + ctx.shootJ + "\n" +
                "FineRoot:    " + ctx.fineRootA + "  " + ctx.fineRootB + "  " + ctx.fineRootJ + "\n" +
                "StrRoot:     " + ctx.structuralRootA + "  " + ctx.structuralRootB + "  " + ctx.structuralRootJ + "\n" +
                "Fruit:       " + ctx.fruitA + "  " + ctx.fruitB + "  " + ctx.fruitJ
            );
        }
    }
]


/* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
//UpdateBranchFlux:	
//backward transport, folding all the carbon flux
/* -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
// UpdateBranchFlux:
// Backward transport, folding all the carbon flux

/**
 * Propagate branch fluxes upstream along each axis (shoot) by folding from
 * terminal {@code Internode}s toward the plant base, aggregating contributions
 * from local sinks and multiple child organs (petioles, fruits, and lateral
 * internodes). Cordon and Trunk nodes are covered implicitly because they
 * subclass {@code Internode}.
 *
 * <p><b>Purpose</b>:
 * Compute per-axis carbon transport terms {@code branch_flux_a} and
 * {@code branch_flux_b} by:
 * <ol>
 *   <li>Seeding the deepest internode in each order with its own sink,
 *       plus all child petiole/fruit fluxes;</li>
 *   <li>Walking upstream via {@code getPredecessor()}, accumulating the
 *       downstream branch (from the node just processed) plus local child
 *       organ fluxes at each upstream internode (including Cordon/Trunk).</li>
 * </ol>
 *
 * <p><b>Key features</b>:
 * <ul>
 *   <li>Performs per-order, per-rank folding of internodes.</li>
 *   <li>Handles structural root folding layer-by-layer via parent links.</li>
 *   <li>Combines both shoot and root carbon fluxes at the PlantBase.</li>
 *   <li>Uses {@code foldTick} to prevent multiple writes within one iteration.</li>
 * </ul>
 *
 * <p><b>Integration</b>:
 * Call this after all sink/source terms are computed for the current time step
 * and before any reporting or forward transport operations.
 * 
 * @since 2025-08
 */

// Add a global flag to control debug_CT output


static int foldTick = 0;
static void updateBranchFlux(PlantBase pb, CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx) [
   {
		  long scopedOrganCount = count((* g:GrowingOrgan, (
		    g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
		  ) *));
		  if (scopedOrganCount > 0) {
		    int persistedFoldStep = max((* g:GrowingOrgan, (
		      g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
		    ) *)[lastFoldStep]);
		    if (foldTick < persistedFoldStep) foldTick = persistedFoldStep;
		  }
		  ctx.foldStep = ++foldTick;
		}


		p:Petiole (-->){1,5} l:Leaf, (
		  p.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber &&
		  l.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
		) ::> {
		  if (l.lastFoldStep == ctx.foldStep) {
			if (debug_CT)
				println("WARN(FOLD): double write Leaf id=" + l.getId());
		  } else {
			p.branch_flux_a += l.branch_flux_a;
			p.branch_flux_b += l.branch_flux_b;
			l.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;     // mark leaf as folded this tick
		  }

		  if (p.lastFoldStep == ctx.foldStep) {
			if (debug_CT) println("WARN(FOLD): double write Petiole id=" + p.getId());
		  }
		  p.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;       // petiole participates this tick
		  p.Update_Branch_Flux();
		}

		p:Petiole (-->){1,5} l:Leaf, (
		  p.rank != l.rank &&
		  p.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber &&
		  l.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
		) ::> {
	  if (debug_CT) {
		println("WARN(CT-LEAF): Petiole-Leaf rank mismatch"
			+ " petioleId=" + p.getId()
			+ " petioleRank=" + p.rank
			+ " leafId=" + l.getId()
			+ " leafRank=" + l.rank
			+ " leafType=" + l.organType
			+ " leafParentID=" + l.parentID
			+ " petioleParentID=" + p.parentID);
	  }
	}


  // ---- INTERNODE FOLD (level-based, no double counting) ----
  {
    long scopedInternodeCount = count((* it:Internode, (
      it.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) *));
    if (scopedInternodeCount > 0) {
    int minOrder = min((* it:Internode, (
      it.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) *)[order]);
    int maxOrder = max((* it:Internode, (
      it.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) *)[order]);
    
    for (int o = maxOrder; o >= minOrder; o--) {
      if (count((* it:Internode, (
        it.order == o &&
        it.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)) == 0) continue;

      int minRank = min((* it:Internode, (
        it.order == o &&
        it.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[rank]);
      int maxRank = max((* it:Internode, (
        it.order == o &&
        it.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[rank]);

      for (int r = maxRank; r >= minRank; r--) {
        [
          nd:Internode, (
            nd.order == o && nd.rank == r &&
            nd.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
          ) ::> {
            if (nd.lastFoldStep == ctx.foldStep && debug_CT) {
              println("WARN(FOLD): double write Internode id=" + nd.getId()
                      + " order=" + o + " rank=" + r);
            }
            nd.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;

            double sumA = nd.sink_source_a;
            double sumB = nd.sink_source_b;
            int k, n;

            n = nd.getChildInternodeCount();
            for (k = 0; k < n; k++) {
              long cid = nd.getChildInternodeIdAt(k);
              Internode ch = nd.getInternode(cid);
              if (ch != null &&
                  ch.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber) {
                sumA += ch.branch_flux_a;
                sumB += ch.branch_flux_b;
                if (ch.lastFoldStep != ctx.foldStep && debug_CT) {
                  println("ERROR(FOLD): child int id=" + ch.getId()
                          + " not folded before parent id=" + nd.getId()
                          + " (order=" + o + " rank=" + r + ")");
                }
              }
            }

           // Petioles
			n = nd.getChildPetioleCount();
			for (k = 0; k < n; k++) {
			  long pid = nd.getChildPetioleIdAt(k);
			  Petiole p = nd.getPetiole(pid);
				  if (p != null &&
				      p.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber) {
				sumA += p.branch_flux_a;
				sumB += p.branch_flux_b;
					if (p.lastFoldStep != ctx.foldStep && debug_CT) {
				  println("WARN(FOLD): petiole not stamped before parent id=" + nd.getId());
				}
					p.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;
			  }
			}
			
			// Fruits
			n = nd.getChildFruitCount();
			for (k = 0; k < n; k++) {
			  long fid = nd.getChildFruitIdAt(k);
			  FruitService f = nd.getFruit(fid);
				  if (f != null &&
				      f.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber) {
				sumA += f.branch_flux_a;
				sumB += f.branch_flux_b;
					f.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;
			  }
			}
			
			// Flowers
			n = nd.getChildFlowerCount();
			for (k = 0; k < n; k++) {
			  long fid = nd.getChildFlowerIdAt(k);
			  Flower fl = nd.getFlower(fid);
				  if (fl != null &&
				      fl.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber) {
				sumA += fl.branch_flux_a;
				sumB += fl.branch_flux_b;
					fl.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;
			  }
			}
			
			nd.branch_flux_a = sumA;
			nd.branch_flux_b = sumB;
				nd.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;   // stamp this internode itself
			nd.Update_Branch_Flux();
			

          }
        ]
      }
    }
    }
  }
	
		sd:StructuralRoot sdr:FineRoot,
		(sdr.parentID == sd.getId()
		 && sd.frID == sdr.getId()
			 && sd.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
			 && sdr.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
			 && sd.ID == sdr.ID) ::> {
		  sd.branch_flux_a = sd.sink_source_a + sdr.branch_flux_a;
		  sd.branch_flux_b = sd.sink_source_b + sdr.branch_flux_b;
			  sdr.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;   // mark terminal
	  if (debug_CT) println("sd. " + sd.nodeNumber + " sd. " + sd.branch_flux_a);
		  sd.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;    // this SR participated too
	  sd.Update_Branch_Flux();
	}
	
		sd:StructuralRoot,
		( sd.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber &&
		  sd.layer == max((* it:StructuralRoot,
							(it.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber &&
							 it.gridX == sd.gridX &&
							 it.gridY == sd.gridY) *)[layer]) ) ::> {
	
	  StructuralRoot cur = sd;
	  while (cur != null) {
		Organ po = cur.getParent();
		if (po == null) break;
	
			if (po instanceof StructuralRoot) {
			  StructuralRoot par = (StructuralRoot) po;
			  if (par.plantNumber != pb.plantNumber) break;
			  par.branch_flux_a += cur.branch_flux_a;
			  par.branch_flux_b += cur.branch_flux_b;
			  cur.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;   // child SR stamped
			  par.Update_Branch_Flux();
			  par.lastFoldStep = ctx.foldStep;   // parent SR stamped
		  cur = par;
		  continue;
		}
		break;
	  }
	}




		  {
	    StructuralRoot st =  pb.getChildStructuralRoot();
	    if (st != null && (st.plantNumber != pb.plantNumber)) st = null;
	    if(debug_CT) println((st != null) ? ("st: " + st.layer) : "st: none");
    double sdlA = (st!=null) ? st.branch_flux_a : 0.0;
    double sdlB = (st!=null) ? st.branch_flux_b : 0.0;

	    Internode tr = pb.getChildInternode();
	    if (tr != null && (tr.plantNumber != pb.plantNumber)) tr = null;

    double sdrA = (tr!=null) ? tr.branch_flux_a : 0.0;
    double sdrB = (tr!=null) ? tr.branch_flux_b : 0.0;

    pb.branch_flux_a = sdlA + sdrA;
    pb.branch_flux_b = sdlB + sdrB;

    if (debug_CT) {
      println("pb " + pb.branch_flux_a + " sdl " + sdlA + " sdr " + sdrA);
      println("pb " + pb.branch_flux_b + " sdl " + sdlB + " sdr " + sdrB);
	      long totalF = count((* g:GrowingOrgan, (
	        g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
	      ) *));
	      long foldedF = count((* g:GrowingOrgan, (
	        g.lastFoldStep == ctx.foldStep &&
	        g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
	      ) *));
	      println("FOLD COVERAGE: " + foldedF + "/" + totalF);
	      long nFlower = count((* f:Flower, (
	        f.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
	      ) *));
	      long nFlowerFolded = count((* f:Flower, (
	        f.lastFoldStep == ctx.foldStep &&
	        f.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
	      ) *));
      println("CT FLOWER FOLD COVERAGE: flower=" + nFlowerFolded + "/" + nFlower);
    }
  }

	  f:Flower, (
	    f.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
	  ) ::> {
    if (debug_CT) {
      if (f.parentID <= 0) {
        println("WARN(CT-FLOWER): Flower has no transport parent"
          + " flowerId=" + f.getId()
          + " rank=" + f.rank
          + " order=" + f.order
          + " organType=" + f.organType);
      } else {
        Organ flowerParent = f.getParent();
        if (flowerParent == null) {
          println("WARN(CT-FLOWER): Flower parent lookup failed"
            + " flowerId=" + f.getId()
            + " parentID=" + f.parentID);
        } else if (!(flowerParent instanceof Internode)) {
          println("WARN(CT-FLOWER): Flower parent is not transport axis"
            + " flowerId=" + f.getId()
            + " parentID=" + f.parentID
            + " parentClass=" + flowerParent.getClass().getName());
        } else {
          Internode axis = (Internode) flowerParent;
          if (axis.plantNumber != pb.plantNumber) {
            println("WARN(CT-FLOWER): Flower parent belongs to another plant"
              + " flowerId=" + f.getId()
              + " parentID=" + axis.getId());
          } else if (!axis.hasChildFlowerId(f.getId())) {
            println("WARN(CT-FLOWER): Parent missing childFlowerId"
              + " flowerId=" + f.getId()
              + " parentID=" + axis.getId()
              + " flowerRank=" + f.rank
              + " flowerOrder=" + f.order);
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  
]



/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

//group UpdateCarbonPotentialUnfold:

/**
 * UpdateCarbonPotential: UNFOLD from plant base to all child organs
 * 
 * <p><b>Purpose:</b> Calculates the carbon potential (cpb/cpt) of all transport-linked organs
 * from the source (PlantBase) outward to sinks. Each organ's cpt is computed from its upstream cpb
 * using its flux values and resistance parameters (r, xp), enforcing directionality and conservation.</p>
 *
 * <p><b>Method:</b>
 * <ul>
 *   <li>PlantBase is seeded with cp = -A/B.</li>
 *   <li>Trunk and basal StructuralRoot are initialized from PB.cpt.</li>
 *   <li>StructuralRoots unfold by layer (deep to surface), via parent–child link.</li>
 *   <li>Shoots unfold from small → large internode order, rank-wise, using child lists.</li>
 *   <li>Petioles and Fruits are pushed similarly from Internode parent.</li>
 *   <li>Leaf cp is synced from petiole.</li>
 * </ul></p>
 *
 * <p><b>Debug control:</b> All output respects a global <code>debug_CT</code> flag.</p>
 *
 * @since 2025-08
 */
static int unfoldTick = 0;            // monotonic counter

static boolean isFiniteCarbonValue(double v) {
    return !Double.isNaN(v) && !Double.isInfinite(v);
}

static boolean isValidPhi(double phi) {
    return isFiniteCarbonValue(phi) && phi >= CT_PHI_FLOOR;
}

static double safePhi(double value) {
    return isValidPhi(value) ? value : CT_PHI_FLOOR;
}

static double validPlantBasePhiOrFloor(double phi) {
    if (!isValidPhi(phi)) return CT_PHI_FLOOR;
    double sugar = sugarFromCp(phi);
    return (isFiniteCarbonValue(sugar) && sugar >= 0.0) ? phi : CT_PHI_FLOOR;
}

static double retainPlantBasePhi(PlantBase pb, double fallbackPhi, int reason) {
    pb.ctPlantBaseFallbackUsed = 1;
    pb.ctPlantBaseFallbackReason = reason;
    pb.ctPlantBaseFallbackCount++;
    return fallbackPhi;
}

static double solvePlantBasePhi(double branchA, double branchB,
        double previousPhi, PlantBase pb) {
    double fallbackPhi = validPlantBasePhiOrFloor(previousPhi);
    pb.ctPlantBaseFallbackUsed = 0;
    pb.ctPlantBaseFallbackReason = 0;
    pb.ctPlantBaseDenominator = branchB;

    if (!isFiniteCarbonValue(branchA) || !isFiniteCarbonValue(branchB)) {
        return retainPlantBasePhi(pb, fallbackPhi, 1);
    }
    if (Math.abs(branchB) <= CT_PB_B_ABS_MIN) {
        return retainPlantBasePhi(pb, fallbackPhi, 2);
    }

    // Divide only after both folded coefficients and the denominator are accepted.
    double candidate = -branchA / branchB;
    if (!isValidPhi(candidate)) {
        return retainPlantBasePhi(pb, fallbackPhi, 3);
    }

    double sugar = sugarFromCp(candidate);
    if (!isFiniteCarbonValue(sugar) || sugar < 0.0) {
        return retainPlantBasePhi(pb, fallbackPhi, 4);
    }
    return candidate;
}

static void applyGuardedPlantBaseCarbonBoundary(PlantBase pb) {
    double previousPhi = pb.cpt;
    pb.cpb = solvePlantBasePhi(
        pb.branch_flux_a, pb.branch_flux_b, previousPhi, pb);
    pb.cpt = pb.cpb;
    pb.j = pb.branch_flux_a + pb.branch_flux_b * pb.cpt;
    pb.ctPlantBaseResidual = pb.j;
    pb.sugarConcentration_phloem = sugarFromCp(pb.cpt);
    pb.sugarConcentration_phloem_pre = pb.sugarConcentration_phloem;
}

static void updateCarbonPotential(PlantBase pb, CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx)
[
  {
    long scopedOrganCount = count((* g:GrowingOrgan, (
      g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) *));
    if (scopedOrganCount > 0) {
      int persistedUnfoldStep = max((* g:GrowingOrgan, (
        g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[lastUnfoldStep]);
      if (unfoldTick < persistedUnfoldStep) unfoldTick = persistedUnfoldStep;
    }
    ctx.unfoldStep = ++unfoldTick;
  }

  {
    applyGuardedPlantBaseCarbonBoundary(pb);
    //println("pb.cpt: " + pb.cpt + " pb.sugarConcentration_phloem: " + pb.sugarConcentration_phloem);
    if (debug_CT) println("PB A=" + pb.branch_flux_a + " B=" + pb.branch_flux_b + " cpt=" + pb.cpt + " j=" + pb.j);
  }

// --- UNFOLD from PlantBase to Trunk + Structural-Root tree (top-down) ---
{
  // 1) PlantBase → basal StructuralRoot (seed) and Trunk
  StructuralRoot s0 = pb.getChildStructuralRoot();
  if (s0 != null && (s0.plantNumber != pb.plantNumber)) s0 = null;
  if (s0 != null) {
    s0.cpb = pb.cpt;
    s0.cpt = safePhi(s0.cpb * (1 - s0.branch_flux_b * s0.r) - s0.branch_flux_a * s0.r - s0.xp);
    if (debug_CT) println("SR-UNFOLD: basal id=" + s0.getId() + " layer=" + s0.layer + " cpb=" + s0.cpb + " cpt=" + s0.cpt);
    if (s0.lastUnfoldStep == ctx.unfoldStep && debug_CT) println("WARN: double write SR (basal) id=" + s0.getId());
    s0.lastUnfoldStep = ctx.unfoldStep;

    // 2) Top-down traversal of the structural-root tree
    //    (DFS using raw ArrayList for Java 1.5 compatibility)
    java.util.ArrayList stack = new java.util.ArrayList();
    stack.add(s0);

    while (!stack.isEmpty()) {
      StructuralRoot parent = (StructuralRoot) stack.remove(stack.size() - 1);

      int n = parent.getChildStructuralRootCount();
      for (int k = 0; k < n; k++) {
        long cid = parent.getChildStructuralRootIdAt(k);
        StructuralRoot ch = parent.getStructuralRoot(cid);
        if (ch == null ||
            ch.plantNumber != pb.plantNumber) continue;

        ch.cpb = parent.cpt;
        ch.cpt = safePhi(ch.cpb * (1 - ch.branch_flux_b * ch.r) - ch.branch_flux_a * ch.r - ch.xp);

        if (debug_CT) {
          println("SR-UNFOLD: parent id=" + parent.getId() + " L" + parent.layer
                + " -> child id=" + ch.getId() + " L" + ch.layer
                + " | cpb=" + ch.cpb + " cpt=" + ch.cpt);
        }
        if (ch.lastUnfoldStep == ctx.unfoldStep && debug_CT) println("WARN: double write SR id=" + ch.getId());
        ch.lastUnfoldStep = ctx.unfoldStep;

        stack.add(ch);
      }
    }
  } else if (debug_CT) {
    println("SR-UNFOLD: no basal StructuralRoot under PlantBase.");
  }

  // Trunk unfold stays as before
  Internode tr = pb.getChildInternode();
  if (tr != null && (tr.plantNumber != pb.plantNumber)) tr = null;
  if (tr != null) {
    tr.cpb = pb.cpt;
    tr.cpt = safePhi(tr.cpb * (1 - tr.branch_flux_b * tr.r) - tr.branch_flux_a * tr.r - tr.xp);
    if (debug_CT) println("unfolding trunk");
    if (tr.lastUnfoldStep == ctx.unfoldStep && debug_CT) println("WARN: double write trunk id=" + tr.getId());
    tr.lastUnfoldStep = ctx.unfoldStep;
  }
}

// --- UNFOLD: StructuralRoot → FineRoot (terminal) ---
	sd:StructuralRoot sdr:FineRoot,
	(sdr.parentID == sd.getId()
	 && sd.frID == sdr.getId()
	 && sd.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
	 && sdr.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
	 && sd.ID == sdr.ID) ::> {
	  // FineRoot takes cpb from its parent StructuralRoot cpt
	  sdr.cpb = sd.cpt;

  // Standard potential update: cpt = cpb*(1 - B*r) - A*r - xp (clamped)
  sdr.cpt = safePhi(sdr.cpb * (1 - sdr.branch_flux_b * sdr.r)
                            - sdr.branch_flux_a * sdr.r
                            - sdr.xp);

  if (debug_CT) {
    println("FR-UNFOLD: SR id=" + sd.getId() + " L" + sd.layer
          + " -> FR id=" + sdr.getId()
          + " | cpb=" + sdr.cpb + " cpt=" + sdr.cpt);
  }

  // Double-write guard (same pattern as trunk/internodes)
  if (sdr.lastUnfoldStep == ctx.unfoldStep && debug_CT) {
    println("WARN: double write FineRoot id=" + sdr.getId());
  }
  sdr.lastUnfoldStep = ctx.unfoldStep;
}


//unfolding the shoot
  {
    long scopedInternodeCount = count((* it:Internode, (
      it.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) *));
    if (scopedInternodeCount > 0) {
    int minOrder = min((* it:Internode, (
      it.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) *)[order]);
    int maxOrder = max((* it:Internode, (
      it.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) *)[order]);
    for (int o = minOrder; o <= maxOrder; o++) {
      if (count((* it:Internode, (
        it.order == o &&
        it.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)) == 0) continue;
      int minRank = min((* it:Internode, (
        it.order == o &&
        it.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[rank]);
      int maxRank = max((* it:Internode, (
        it.order == o &&
        it.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[rank]);
      for (int r = minRank; r <= maxRank; r++) {
        [ parent:Internode, (
          parent.order == o && parent.rank == r &&
          parent.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
        ) ::> {
          if (debug_CT) println("O" + o + " rank " + r + " id=" + parent.getId() + " cpb=" + parent.cpb + " cpt=" + parent.cpt);
          int k, n;

          n = parent.getChildInternodeCount();
          for (k = 0; k < n; k++) {
            long id = parent.getChildInternodeIdAt(k);
            Internode ch = parent.getInternode(id);
            if (ch != null && ch.parentID == parent.getId() &&
                ch.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber) {
              if (ch.lastUnfoldStep == ctx.unfoldStep && debug_CT) println("WARN: double write Internode id=" + ch.getId());
              ch.lastUnfoldStep = ctx.unfoldStep;
              ch.cpb = parent.cpt;
              ch.cpt = safePhi(ch.cpb * (1 - ch.branch_flux_b * ch.r) - ch.branch_flux_a * ch.r - ch.xp);
              if (debug_CT) println("  -> child int id=" + ch.getId() + " cpb=" + ch.cpb + " cpt=" + ch.cpt);
            }
          }

          n = parent.getChildPetioleCount();
          for (k = 0; k < n; k++) {
            Petiole p = parent.getPetiole(parent.getChildPetioleIdAt(k));
            if (p != null &&
                p.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber) {
              if (p.lastUnfoldStep == ctx.unfoldStep && debug_CT) println("WARN: double write Petiole id=" + p.getId());
              p.lastUnfoldStep = ctx.unfoldStep;
              p.cpb = parent.cpt;
              p.cpt = safePhi(p.cpb * (1 - p.branch_flux_b * p.r) - p.branch_flux_a * p.r - p.xp);
              if (debug_CT) println("  -> child petiole id=" + p.getId() + " cpb=" + p.cpb + " cpt=" + p.cpt);
            }
          }

          n = parent.getChildFruitCount();
          for (k = 0; k < n; k++) {
            FruitService f = parent.getFruit(parent.getChildFruitIdAt(k));
            if (f != null &&
                f.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber) {
              if (f.lastUnfoldStep == ctx.unfoldStep && debug_CT) println("WARN: double write Fruit id=" + f.getId());
              f.lastUnfoldStep = ctx.unfoldStep;
              f.cpb = parent.cpt;
              f.cpt = safePhi(f.cpb);
              if (debug_CT) 
              	  println("  -> child fruit id=" + f.getId() + " cpb=" + f.cpb + " cpt=" + f.cpt);
            }
          }
          
          n = parent.getChildFlowerCount();
          for (k = 0; k < n; k++) {
            Flower fl = parent.getFlower(parent.getChildFlowerIdAt(k));
            if (fl != null &&
                fl.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber) {
              if (fl.lastUnfoldStep == ctx.unfoldStep && debug_CT) println("WARN: double write Flower id=" + fl.getId());
              fl.lastUnfoldStep = ctx.unfoldStep;
              fl.cpb = parent.cpt;
              fl.cpt = safePhi(fl.cpb * (1 - fl.branch_flux_b * fl.r) - fl.branch_flux_a * fl.r - fl.xp);
              if (debug_CT) println("  -> child flower id=" + fl.getId() + " cpb=" + fl.cpb + " cpt=" + fl.cpt);
            }
          }
          
        } ]
      }
    }
    }
  }

	sd:Petiole (-->){1,5} sdr:Leaf, (
	  sd.rank == sdr.rank &&
	  sd.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber &&
	  sdr.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
	) ::> {
	  sd.cpb = safePhi(sd.cpb);
	  sd.cpt = safePhi(sd.cpt);
	
	  sdr.cpb = sd.cpt;
	  sdr.cpt = sdr.cpb;
	  
	  if (sdr.lastUnfoldStep == ctx.unfoldStep && debug_CT) {
		println("WARN: double write Leaf id=" + sdr.getId());
	  }
	  sdr.lastUnfoldStep = ctx.unfoldStep;
	}

	p:Petiole (-->){1,5} l:Leaf, (
	  p.rank != l.rank &&
	  p.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber &&
	  l.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
	) ::> {
	  if (debug_CT) {
		println("WARN(CT-LEAF): Petiole-Leaf rank mismatch"
			+ " petioleId=" + p.getId()
			+ " petioleRank=" + p.rank
			+ " leafId=" + l.getId()
			+ " leafRank=" + l.rank
			+ " leafType=" + l.organType
			+ " leafParentID=" + l.parentID
			+ " petioleParentID=" + p.parentID);
	  }
	}

  {
    if (debug_CT) 
    {
      long total = count((* g:GrowingOrgan, (
        g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *));
      long unfolded = count((* g:GrowingOrgan, (
        g.lastUnfoldStep == ctx.unfoldStep &&
        g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *));
      println("UNFOLD COVERAGE: " + unfolded + "/" + total);
      long nLeaf = count((* l:Leaf, (
        l.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *));
      long nLeafUnfolded = count((* l:Leaf, (
        l.lastUnfoldStep == ctx.unfoldStep &&
        l.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *));
      long nRosetteLeaf = count((* l:Leaf, (
        "rosetteLeaf".equals(l.organType) &&
        l.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *));
      long nRosetteLeafUnfolded = count((* l:Leaf, (
        "rosetteLeaf".equals(l.organType) &&
        l.lastUnfoldStep == ctx.unfoldStep &&
        l.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *));
      println("CT LEAF UNFOLD COVERAGE: leaf=" + nLeafUnfolded + "/" + nLeaf
        + " rosette=" + nRosetteLeafUnfolded + "/" + nRosetteLeaf);
      long nFlower = count((* f:Flower, (
        f.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *));
      long nFlowerUnfolded = count((* f:Flower, (
        f.lastUnfoldStep == ctx.unfoldStep &&
        f.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *));
      println("CT FLOWER UNFOLD COVERAGE: flower=" + nFlowerUnfolded + "/" + nFlower);
  	}
}

	l:Leaf, (
	  l.lastUnfoldStep != ctx.unfoldStep &&
	  l.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
	) ::> {
	  if (debug_CT) {
		println("WARN(CT-LEAF): Leaf not unfolded"
			+ " leafId=" + l.getId()
			+ " rank=" + l.rank
			+ " organType=" + l.organType
			+ " parentID=" + l.parentID);
	  }
	}

	f:Flower, (
	  f.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
	) ::> {
	  if (debug_CT) {
		if (f.parentID <= 0) {
		  println("WARN(CT-FLOWER): Flower has no transport parent"
			+ " flowerId=" + f.getId()
			+ " rank=" + f.rank
			+ " order=" + f.order
			+ " organType=" + f.organType);
		} else {
		  Organ flowerParent = f.getParent();
		  if (flowerParent == null) {
			println("WARN(CT-FLOWER): Flower parent lookup failed"
			  + " flowerId=" + f.getId()
			  + " parentID=" + f.parentID);
		  } else if (!(flowerParent instanceof Internode)) {
			println("WARN(CT-FLOWER): Flower parent is not transport axis"
			  + " flowerId=" + f.getId()
			  + " parentID=" + f.parentID
			  + " parentClass=" + flowerParent.getClass().getName());
			  } else {
				Internode axis = (Internode) flowerParent;
				if (axis.plantNumber != pb.plantNumber) {
				  println("WARN(CT-FLOWER): Flower parent belongs to another plant"
					+ " flowerId=" + f.getId()
					+ " parentID=" + axis.getId());
				} else if (!axis.hasChildFlowerId(f.getId())) {
			  println("WARN(CT-FLOWER): Parent missing childFlowerId"
				+ " flowerId=" + f.getId()
				+ " parentID=" + axis.getId()
				+ " flowerRank=" + f.rank
				+ " flowerOrder=" + f.order);
			}
		  }
		}
		if (Double.isNaN(f.cpt) || Double.isInfinite(f.cpt) || f.cpt < 0.0) {
		  println("WARN(CT-FLOWER): Invalid flower cpt"
			+ " flowerId=" + f.getId()
			+ " cpt=" + f.cpt
			+ " parentID=" + f.parentID);
		}
	  }
	}

]

/** --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * UpdateFlow — one Newton step that updates each organ’s linearized
 * source/sink flux j using the current local carbon potential (cpt).
 *
 * <p><b>What it does</b>
 * <ul>
 *   <li>For every GrowingOrgan <code>sd</code>, computes the new flux
 *       <code>new_j = sd.sink_source_a + sd.sink_source_b * sd.cpt</code>,
 *       i.e. the first-order (Taylor) linearization of the Michaelis–Menten
 *       sink/source function with respect to carbon potential Φ (stored here
 *       as <code>cpt</code> at the “top” side of the transport segment).</li>
 *   <li>Saves the residual <code>sd.err = new_j - sd.j</code> and accumulates
 *       it into the per-call convergence residual.</li>
 *   <li>Applies a small-current threshold <code>EPSILON</code> and clamps
 *       near-zero fluxes to 0 for numerical stability.</li>
 *   <li>Guards against invalid carbon potentials: if <code>cpt &lt; 0</code> or
 *       NaN/Inf, reset to a small positive value.</li>
 *   <li>Calls <code>derive()</code> to update derived state after flux changes.</li>
 * </ul>
 *
 * <p><b>Sign & units</b>
 * <ul>
 *   <li><code>sd.j</code> is the net <em>mass carbon transport</em> for that organ
 *       (gC·h⁻¹). Convention: <em>positive</em> j = unloading from phloem to the organ
 *       (sink); <em>negative</em> j = loading from organ to phloem (source).</li>
 *   <li><code>sd.sink_source_a</code>, <code>sd.sink_source_b</code> are the linear
 *       coefficients a, b from the Taylor expansion of the sink/source law
 *       around Φ₀, i.e. <code>j ≈ a + b Φ</code>.</li>
 * </ul>
 *
 * <p><b>Background</b>
 * In the coupled phloem/xylem transport (CT) model, we solve mass flux
 * using the “carbon potential” Φ ≝ c²/2 so that the transport law is linear
 * in dΦ/dx. Organs’ nonlinear sink/source laws are linearized as
 * <code>j = a + b Φ</code> for each iteration of the global solve.
 * See: definition of Φ and j, transport equation, and linearization of
 * sink functions with a and b. 
 * -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
static void updateFlow(PlantBase pb, CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx)
[
  sd:GrowingOrgan, (
    sd.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
  ) ::>
  {
    double new_j = 0.0;

    if (sd.cpt >= 0.0 && !Double.isNaN(sd.cpt) && !Double.isInfinite(sd.cpt)) {
      // Linearized sink/source: j = a + b * Φ (Φ stored as cpt here)
      new_j = sd.sink_source_a + sd.sink_source_b * sd.cpt;

      // Residual for this organ and accumulate absolute error
      sd.err = new_j - sd.j;
      ctx.convergenceError += Math.abs(sd.err);
      // Threshold very small currents for stability
      if (Math.abs(new_j) < EPSILON) {
        sd.j = 0.0;
      } else {
        sd.j = new_j;
      }
    } else {
      // Invalid Φ: reset and penalize residual to keep the solver progressing
      sd.cpt = 1e-5;
      sd.err = 1.0;
      ctx.convergenceError += 1.0;
    }

    
    if (debug_CT) {
      println(
        "sd." + sd.nodeNumber +
        " j="   + sd.j +
        " cpt=" + sd.cpt +
        " cpb=" + sd.cpb +
        " sink_a=" + sd.sink_source_a +
        " sink_b=" + sd.sink_source_b
      );
    }
  }

  
 {
  if (debug_CT) {
 //if(true) {
    println(
      "Iter " + ctx.iterationCount +
      " | sumj=" + sum((* g:GrowingOrgan, (
        g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[j]) +
      " | sum|j|=" + sum(Math.abs((* g:GrowingOrgan, (
        g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[j])) +
      " | internode=" + sum((* g:Internode, (
        g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[j]) +
      " | structuralRoot=" + sum((* g:StructuralRoot, (
        g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[j]) +
      " | Leaf=" + sum((* g:Leaf, (
        g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[j]) +
      " | Fruit=" + sum((* g:FruitService, (
        g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
      ) *)[j])
    );
    
   // After updateFlow() + convergence, add:

  double sumJ = sum((* g:GrowingOrgan, (
    g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
  ) *)[j]);
  double pbJ  = pb.j;
  double net  = sumJ + pbJ;

  println("CLOSURE CHECK  sum(j_organs)=" + sumJ
        + "  pb.j=" + pbJ
        + "  net=" + net);
 
  }
 }
]


/**
 * Refresh transport resistances and related parameters per organ.
 *
 * <p>Derives phloem carbon concentration {@code c = sqrt(2*cpt)} and invokes
 * {@code updateCTRs(c)} to refresh local resistance {@code r}, osmotic terms, and
 * any transport coefficients dependent on concentration.</p>
 *
 * @implNote The method name is kept as {@code updateResistence()} for backward compatibility.
 * @since 2025-08
 */


static void updateResistence(PlantBase pb)
[
 
	 g:GrowingOrgan, (
	   g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
	 ) ::>
	{
	  double carbon = Math.sqrt(2.0 * g.cpt);	
	  g.updateCTRs(carbon);
	  //test xp
	 // g.xp = 0;
	}
	
]
/**
 * Update organ-level carbon status after the transport solve.
 *
 * <p><b>Actions</b>
 * <ul>
 *   <li>Compute phloem carbon concentration and sugar units from {@code cpt}.</li>
 *   <li>Re-evaluate loading, leakage, and unloading terms in sugar space.</li>
 *   <li>Store {@code Cflux = j / mgTogram} for reporting (guard NaN).</li>
 *   <li>Refresh transport coefficients via {@code updateCTRs(carbon)}.</li>
 *   <li>Compute Munch counter flow {@code Mcf} using branch flux and local concentration.</li>
 * </ul></p>
 *
 * <p><b>Guards</b> — NaNs in branch flux or Mcf are replaced with small defaults.</p>
 *
 * @since 2025-08
 */

static void updateCarbonStatus(PlantBase pb)
[
	//group develop 
	//{ double maxCp = max((*S *)[cpb]);}
	 
	 g:GrowingOrgan, (
	   g.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
	 ) ::> {
		  double carbon = Math.sqrt(2.0 * g.cpt);
		  double sugar = convertPhloemCtoSugar(carbon);
		  
		  g.updateCarbonAllocation(sugar);
		  
		  g.Cflux = g.j * 1/mgTogram;	
		  if(Double.isNaN(g.Cflux)) g.Cflux = 1e-6;
		  //  s.cpt = s.cpb = maxCp;
		   
		  //s.cpb = s.cpt = max();  
		  g.updateCTRs(carbon);
		
		  // Effect of phloem flux on hydraulic flow: Munch counter flow (following Equation 5) 
		  //checked the original code McF do use cpb in the calculation. 
		  double branchj = g.branch_flux_a + g.branch_flux_b * g.cpb;
		  if(Double.isNaN(branchj)) { branchj = 1e-5;}
		 
		  g.Mcf = MolalVolumeSucrose * branchj - branchj / carbon;
		 
		  if(Double.isNaN(g.Mcf)) g.Mcf = 0;
		}
		
	 {
	 	pb.updateCarbonPartition();
	 }
		
		
]


/**
 * Write compact carbon-transport mass-balance diagnostics for each solved step.
 *
 * <p>Flux columns are diagnostic-only sums of solved organ fluxes: loading is
 * the absolute value of negative source fluxes and unloading is the sum of
 * positive sink fluxes. No explicit storage/boundary term is available here,
 * so netFluxResidual is reported as totalLoading - totalUnloading.</p>
 */
static void writeCtMassBalanceDiagnostics(PlantBase pb, int iterationCount, double convergenceError) {
  long organCount = count((* gCount:GrowingOrgan, (
    gCount.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
  ) *));
  double totalLoading = Math.abs(sum((* gLoad:GrowingOrgan, (
    gLoad.j < 0.0 &&
    gLoad.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
  ) *)[j]));
  double totalUnloading = sum((* gUnload:GrowingOrgan, (
    gUnload.j > 0.0 &&
    gUnload.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
  ) *)[j]);
  double netFluxResidual = totalLoading - totalUnloading;
  double relativeFluxResidual = Math.abs(netFluxResidual)
      / Math.max(Math.max(Math.abs(totalLoading), Math.abs(totalUnloading)), 1e-12);

  double minCp = 0.0;
  double maxCp = 0.0;
  double meanCp = 0.0;
  double minSugar = 0.0;
  double maxSugar = 0.0;
  double meanSugar = 0.0;
  if (organCount > 0) {
    minCp = min((* gMin:GrowingOrgan, (
      gMin.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) *)[cpt]);
    maxCp = max((* gMax:GrowingOrgan, (
      gMax.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) *)[cpt]);
    meanCp = mean((* gMean:GrowingOrgan, (
      gMean.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
    ) *)[cpt]);
    minSugar = sugarFromCp(minCp);
    maxSugar = sugarFromCp(maxCp);
    // Diagnostic mean sugar is computed from mean Phi to keep this source-only patch
    // compatible with older RGG aggregate-expression parsing.
    meanSugar = sugarFromCp(meanCp);
  }

  CarbonTransportMassBalanceDiagnosticOutputData row =
      new CarbonTransportMassBalanceDiagnosticOutputData();
  row.timestamp = timestamp;
  row.step = step;
  row.year = year;
  row.dayOfYear = dayOfYear;
  row.hourOfDay = hourOfDay;
  row.scenario = scenario;
  row.simuuid = simUUID;
  row.plantNumber = pb.plantNumber;
  row.fieldInstanceId = pb.fieldInstanceId;
  row.day = day;
  row.hour = hourOfDay;
  row.useCPStyleCTResponse = true;
  row.iterationCount = iterationCount;
  row.convergenceError = convergenceError;
  row.totalLoading = totalLoading;
  row.totalUnloading = totalUnloading;
  row.netFluxResidual = netFluxResidual;
  row.relativeFluxResidual = relativeFluxResidual;
  row.minCp = minCp;
  row.maxCp = maxCp;
  row.meanCp = meanCp;
  row.minSugar = minSugar;
  row.maxSugar = maxSugar;
  row.meanSugar = meanSugar;
  row.ctPlantBaseFallbackUsed = pb.ctPlantBaseFallbackUsed;
  row.ctPlantBaseFallbackReason = pb.ctPlantBaseFallbackReason;
  row.ctPlantBaseFallbackCount = pb.ctPlantBaseFallbackCount;
  row.ctPlantBaseResidual = pb.ctPlantBaseResidual;
  row.ctPlantBaseDenominator = pb.ctPlantBaseDenominator;
  DiagnosticTableCoordinator.writeCarbonTransportMassBalance(row);
}

/**
 * Execute one full carbon-transport solve for the current time step.
 *
 * <p><b>Sequence</b>
 * <ol>
 *   <li>{@link #linearise(PlantBase, CarbonTransportSolveContext)} — per-organ (a,b)</li>
 *   <li>{@link #updateBranchFlux(PlantBase, CarbonTransportSolveContext)} — fold to branch (a,b)</li>
 *   <li>{@link #updateCarbonPotential(PlantBase, CarbonTransportSolveContext)} — unfold cp across the plant graph</li>
 *   <li>{@link #updateFlow(PlantBase, CarbonTransportSolveContext)} — update j and residuals</li>
 *   <li>{@link #updateResistence(PlantBase)} — refresh transport coefficients</li>
 *   <li>Repeat steps 1–5 while the residual exceeds {@code MAXERROR} and the
 *       iteration count is at most 20; print diagnostics if {@code printFlag}.</li>
 *   <li>{@link #updateCarbonStatus(PlantBase)} — final per-organ status & Mcf.</li>
 * </ol></p>
 *
 * <p><b>Convergence control</b>
 * <ul>
 *   <li>The per-call convergence error is the sum of absolute per-organ residuals.</li>
 *   <li>{@code MAXERROR} and the per-call iteration count bound the iteration.</li>
 *   <li>On excessive passes (e.g., 200), fallback assigns {@code j = a + b·cpt}
 *       and stops the run safely.</li>
 * </ul></p>
 *
 * <p><b>Scope</b> — Only organs matching the supplied plant identity are read or updated.</p>
 *
 * @since 2025-08
 */

static void updateC_Transport(PlantBase pb)
{
		if (pb == null) {
			throw new IllegalArgumentException("Carbon transport requires a PlantBase instance.");
		}
		CarbonTransportSolveContext ctx = new CarbonTransportSolveContext();

		//waterFlowEst();
		//waterPotential();
		linearise(pb, ctx);
		updateBranchFlux(pb, ctx);
		updateCarbonPotential(pb, ctx);
		updateFlow(pb, ctx);
		updateResistence(pb);
		//
		while((ctx.convergenceError > MAXERROR ) && ctx.iterationCount <= 20)
		{
			ctx.iterationCount++;
			ctx.convergenceError = 0.0;
			linearise(pb, ctx);
			updateBranchFlux(pb, ctx);
			updateCarbonPotential(pb, ctx);
			updateFlow(pb, ctx);
			updateResistence(pb);
			if (debug && printFlag) { println("error_count " + ctx.iterationCount + " Serror " + ctx.convergenceError); }
			if (debug && printFlag) {
				double sumFlux = sum((* gFlux:GrowingOrgan, (
				  gFlux.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
				) *)[j]);
				double sumAbsFlux = sum(Math.abs((* gAbsFlux:GrowingOrgan, (
				  gAbsFlux.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
				) *)[j]));
				println("sumFlux " + sumFlux);
				println("RelativeError " + ((sumAbsFlux > 0.0) ? sumFlux / sumAbsFlux : 0.0));
			}

			if (ctx.iterationCount > 20) // too many passes?
	        {	// report problem
	        [
	         sd:GrowingOrgan, (
	           sd.err > MAXERROR &&
	           sd.plantNumber == pb.plantNumber
	         ) ::>
         {
			sd.j = sd.sink_source_a + sd.sink_source_b * sd.cpt; 
         	 //if (printFlag) { println("rank " + sd.rank  + " j " + sd.j + " cpt " + sd.cpt + " err " + sd.err); }
		 }
		]
		 if (debug && printFlag) { println("carbon transport does not convergening well"); }
		 
		 //continueRunning = false;
		 
		// break;
        }
      

		}
		updateCarbonStatus(pb);
		if(outputCarbonTransportDiagnostics) {
			writeCtMassBalanceDiagnostics(pb, ctx.iterationCount, ctx.convergenceError);
		}


	}




/**
 * Utilities for coupling xylem pull with phloem transport in the linearised
 * carbon-potential (Φ) framework.
 *
 * <h3>Conventions</h3>
 * <ul>
 *   <li>Local linearisation: {@code j ≈ a + b·Φ} at the distal (downstream) end of a segment.</li>
 *   <li>Potential drop across one segment: {@code Φ_top = Φ_bot − r·j − x_p}.</li>
 *   <li><b>This class stores</b> {@code x_p ≥ 0} as an extra drop (magnitude only).</li>
 *   <li>If you instead store Alla’s signed pull {@code x_p^{(−)} ≤ 0}, use the notes under each method.</li>
 * </ul>
 */
  /**
   * Exact <b>UNFOLD</b>: compute the top potential {@code cpt} from the bottom potential {@code cpb}
   * through one transport segment with resistance {@code r}, distal linearisation {@code (a,b)},
   * and xylem pull magnitude {@code x_p ≥ 0}.
   *
   * <p><b>Governing relations</b></p>
   * <pre>
   * j = a + b·cpt
   * cpt = cpb − r·j − x_p
   * </pre>
   *
   * <p><b>Derivation</b></p>
   * Substitute the first into the second:
   * <pre>
   * cpt = cpb − r·(a + b·cpt) − x_p
   * (1 + b·r)·cpt = cpb − a·r − x_p
   * </pre>
   * Hence the exact unfold:
   * <pre>
   * cpt = (cpb − a·r − x_p) / (1 + b·r)
   * </pre>
   *
   * <p><b>Alla’s convention (optional)</b> — if you store {@code x_p^{(−)} ≤ 0} (signed pull),
   * pass {@code x_p = -x_p^{(−)}} here, or use the equivalent form
   * {@code cpt = (cpb − a·r − x_p^{(−)})/(1 + b·r)}.</p>
   *
   * @param cpb bottom carbon potential Φ (segment inlet)
   * @param a   distal intercept of j–Φ linearisation (units of flux)
   * @param b   distal slope of j–Φ linearisation (per-Φ)
   * @param r   segment phloem resistance (Φ per unit flux)
   * @param xp  xylem-pull magnitude (extra drop) {@code x_p ≥ 0}
   * @return    top carbon potential Φ: {@code cpt = (cpb − a·r − x_p)/(1 + b·r)}
   */
   //not sure why but actually the first order expansion works better than the exact form
   //maybe due to the whole method is using linear operation
  public static double unfoldPhi(double cpb, double a, double b, double r, double xp) {
    return (cpb - a * r - xp) / (1.0 + b * r);
  }

  /**
   * Exact <b>FOLD</b>: map distal linear coefficients {@code (a,b)} through one segment
   * to an upstream view {@code (a', b')} such that {@code j = a' + b'·cpb}.
   *
   * <p><b>Derivation</b></p>
   * Start with {@code j = a + b·cpt} and plug the exact unfold:
   * <pre>
   * j = a + b·(cpb − a·r − x_p)/(1 + b·r)
   *   = [a + b·cpb − b·x_p] / (1 + b·r)
   *   = a' + b'·cpb
   * </pre>
   * Therefore,
   * <pre>
   * a' = (a − b·x_p) / (1 + b·r)
   * b' =  b         / (1 + b·r)
   * </pre>
   *
   * <p><b>Sanity check</b> — With these {@code a', b'} and the unfold above,
   * {@code a + b·cpt ≡ a' + b'·cpb} (identity), which preserves mass balance and improves stability.</p>
   *
   * <p><b>Alla’s convention (optional)</b> — if you store {@code x_p^{(−)} ≤ 0}, use
   * {@code a' = (a + b·x_p^{(−)})/(1 + b·r)} (the “plus” seen in her code), with the same {@code b'}.</p>
   *
   * @param a  distal intercept
   * @param b  distal slope
   * @param r  segment resistance
   * @param xp xylem-pull magnitude (extra drop) {@code x_p ≥ 0}
   * @return   a 2-element array {@code [a', b']} (upstream coefficients)
   */
  public static double[] foldCoeffs(double a, double b, double r, double xp) {
    double denom = 1.0 + b * r;
    double aPrime = (a - b * xp) / denom;
    double bPrime =  b / denom;
    return new double[] { aPrime, bPrime };
  }
